  "arrangerNotes": "Verified against the LilyPond score on Hungarian Wikipedia (8 bars with a repeat sign, written out: once for verse 1, once for the chorus, as the song is sung). The English verse/chorus words fit the notes syllable for syllable. No simplification needed. Range low 5 to 5. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–7 of Percy Montrose's song as printed in Henry Randall Waite's College Songs (1887), from Wikisource (https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/College_Songs/Oh_My_Darling_Clementine); the source's 'canon' (cañon) in verse 5 is spelled 'canyon' as in verse 1. The chorus is sung after every verse. Per-verse notes (verseLines): verses 4 and 5 have 16 syllables in their second line, one more than its 15 notes, so one quarter note is played as two eighths of the same pitch ('swim-mer' in verse 4; 'roses, and' in verse 5).",
  "verified": true
}
